      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a dose that predictably risks severe or fatal liver injury. For a 70 kg adult, that's well above the single-dose and daily limits (about 15 mg/kg per dose and 4 g/day), and I don't know of any indication that justifies it. Normal baseline liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day).\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n\nIf you think this dose is clinically needed, for example because of a protocol I don't know about, please take it up directly with pharmacy or toxicology. If the order needs to go in, it should be entered through a pathway with pharmacist review, not through me.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the alternatives?"
      }
